{"requirements":[{"id":"radius_configuration","requirement":"Configure node1 to provide RADIUS authentication for node2 using a dedicated node2 client secret and the demonstration user from access.txt.","status":"satisfied","summary":"FreeRADIUS is active and enabled on node1, listens on UDP/1812, and has a client restricted to node2's address. Configuration validation succeeded, and the installed user entry was directly compared with access.txt. A generated client secret was securely installed on both nodes.","evidence_ids":["cmd-01458b7654f648e8","cmd-f86cf64ea925475a","cmd-14cc4eb2e5194719","cmd-413e1833282d4447"]},{"id":"authentication_behavior","requirement":"Correct credentials must receive Access-Accept, wrong credentials Access-Reject, and requests using the wrong client secret must not be accepted.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Tests originating from node2 directly observed Access-Accept for the configured credentials and Access-Reject for an incorrect password. The wrong-secret test logic explicitly failed on Access-Accept and completed successfully. These outcomes were repeated after both node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-204fbe52fbba4b77","cmd-4aae789b76c8464f","cmd-a549fd6765a2471d"]},{"id":"handover_integrity","requirement":"Keep /srv/legacy2/radius-network-authentication intact.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final SHA-256 hashes of access.txt and client-notes.txt on both nodes exactly match the authored preparation baseline; those were the only regular files recorded in the handover directory.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","seeded-state-node2","cmd-413e1833282d4447","cmd-9074f8928251470f"]},{"id":"legacy_platform_preservation","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained RHEL 7.9 on kernel 3.10.0-1160.el7.x86_64. The installed FreeRADIUS packages are EL7 builds at version 3.0.13-15.el7.","evidence_ids":["global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_prepare:node2:platform","cmd-0d91e7eab9cb425b","cmd-8c9edb9ffc7a406f","cmd-413e1833282d4447","cmd-9074f8928251470f","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.96,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.84,"summary":"The functional mutations were well-scoped, services were healthy, no failed units remained, repositories were returned to disabled state, and both restart protocols were complete. Minor executor-created residue remained: three manually downloaded RPMs on node1 from cmd-ae773d0d321741af; temporary downloaded GPG-key sources on node1 and node2 from cmd-395c8670cbd24a0b and cmd-91f2938961934648; /tmp/radius-check.out from cmd-a19c68cc70464e40 and cmd-3e18ba0fc5dd47d8; and reboot logs from cmd-d69f454a681c4bb3 and cmd-2fb96862b0124c1c. These low-risk artifacts were not cleaned. No unnecessary mutation is shown as reverted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ae773d0d321741af","cmd-395c8670cbd24a0b","cmd-91f2938961934648","cmd-a19c68cc70464e40","cmd-3e18ba0fc5dd47d8","cmd-d69f454a681c4bb3","cmd-2fb96862b0124c1c","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. RADIUS behavior was directly exercised from node2 and persisted through sequential restarts. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered system/service or client state, preserved handover data, and successful post-restart authentication. Lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate both restarts.","limitations":["Native package-manager health checks timed out before preparation and after execution, so final RPM database consistency was not independently established.","Wrong-secret result text is redacted in captured output, although the visible test logic proves that an Access-Accept would have caused failure and the commands completed successfully."]}
